sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Staff user
    participant UI as Login screen
    participant AU as Auth service<br/>(Laravel Fortify)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant RB as RBAC resolver
    participant AL as Audit Log

    Note over U,AL: Two-factor is mandatory for Super Admin and Finance only -<br/>the two roles that hold payment credentials and approve settlements.

    U->>UI: email + password
    UI->>AU: attempt(credentials)
    AU->>DB: load user by email

    alt account suspended
        DB-->>AU: status = suspended
        AU->>AL: log failed attempt (reason = suspended)
        AU-->>UI: generic "invalid credentials"
        Note right of AU: The message never reveals whether<br/>the account exists or is suspended -<br/>that would confirm valid emails<br/>to an attacker.
    else password incorrect
        AU->>AU: increment failed counter
        AU->>AL: log failed attempt
        alt 5 failures within 15 minutes
            AU-->>UI: account locked, retry later
        else
            AU-->>UI: invalid credentials
        end
    else password correct
        AU->>RB: resolve role for this user
        RB-->>AU: role + capability set

        alt role requires 2FA (Super Admin or Finance)
            AU-->>UI: challenge - TOTP required
            U->>UI: 6-digit authenticator code
            UI->>AU: verify(code)
            alt code invalid or expired
                AU->>AL: log failed 2FA
                AU-->>UI: reject, allow retry
            else code valid
                AU->>DB: create session (device, IP, expiry)
                AU->>AL: log successful sign-in + 2FA
            end
        else 2FA not required
            AU->>DB: create session (device, IP, expiry)
            AU->>AL: log successful sign-in
        end
    end

    AU-->>UI: session established
    UI->>RB: build navigation for this role
    RB-->>UI: only permitted routes

    Note over UI,RB: The sidebar is generated from the same capability<br/>set the guard enforces, so a link can never appear<br/>that the guard would then refuse.

    U->>UI: request a screen
    UI->>RB: allowed(route, role)?
    alt permitted
        RB-->>UI: render screen
    else not permitted
        RB->>AL: log refused access (user, route, timestamp)
        RB-->>UI: refusal panel, not a blank page
    end

    Note over DB,AL: Idle sessions expire after 60 minutes.<br/>Suspending a user revokes every active session<br/>immediately, but their audit history is retained -<br/>deleting a user would orphan every action they took.
